The provided `ForEachWhileObserver` is a thin wrapper that delegates to user‑supplied `Predicate`, `Consumer`, and `Action` callbacks and manages a disposable reference. Its behavior and performance are heavily dependent on those external functions and the upstream RxJava flow, not on intrinsic algorithmic work within the class itself. Consequently, a standalone JMH benchmark would not yield meaningful or reproducible performance data for this component.